{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,10]],"date-time":"2026-10-10T01:27:45Z","timestamp":1791595665185,"version":"4.3.4"},"reference-count":48,"publisher":"Cambridge University Press (CUP)","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2022,10,18]],"date-time":"2022-10-18T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1666051200000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["cambridge.org"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["J. Fluid Mech."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2022,11,10]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>We consider steady, fully-developed flows of deformable, inelastic grains driven by gravity between identical bumpy walls. Using constitutive relations from extended kinetic theory (EKT) for the erodible bed near the centreline and the collisional flow between the surfaces of the bed and the walls, we calculate the fields of mean velocity, fluctuation velocity and solid volume fraction across the chute. We consider both situations in which the solid volume fraction at and near the centreline is high enough to form a bed and when it is not. We compare results predicted by EKT with recent discrete element simulations results, and obtain very good agreement.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1017\/jfm.2022.807","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2022,10,18]],"date-time":"2022-10-18T12:19:30Z","timestamp":1666095570000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/policypage","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":10,"title":["Extended kinetic theory for granular flow in a vertical chute"],"prefix":"10.1017","volume":"950","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-4140-5798","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Mudasir Ul","family":"Islam","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-9731-0528","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"J. T.","family":"Jenkins","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-1301-4255","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"S. L.","family":"Das","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"56","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2022,10,18]]},"reference":[{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref5","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"4799","DOI":"10.1039\/C5SM00337G","article-title":"Steady shearing flows of deformable, inelastic spheres","volume":"11","author":"Berzi","year":"2015","journal-title":"Soft Matter"},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref8","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","DOI":"10.1017\/jfm.2019.1017","article-title":"Extended kinetic theory for granular flow over and within an inclined erodible bed","volume":"885","author":"Berzi","year":"2020","journal-title":"J. Fluid Mech."},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref12","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"070603","DOI":"10.1063\/1.4812804","article-title":"A modified kinetic theory for frictional granular flows in dense and dilute regimes","volume":"25","author":"Chialvo","year":"2013","journal-title":"Phys. Fluids"},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref21","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1","DOI":"10.1016\/0020-7462(94)90047-7","article-title":"Flow of granular materials down a vertical pipe","volume":"29","author":"Gudhe","year":"1994","journal-title":"Intl J. Non-Linear Mech."},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref22","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"401","DOI":"10.1017\/S0022112083003419","article-title":"Grain flow as a fluid-mechanical phenomenon","volume":"134","author":"Haff","year":"1983","journal-title":"J. Fluid Mech."},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref35","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"031305","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevE.75.031305","article-title":"Velocity correlations in dense granular shear flows: effects on energy dissipation and normal stress","volume":"75","author":"Mitarai","year":"2007","journal-title":"Phys. Rev. E"},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref44","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"2337","DOI":"10.1063\/1.869012","article-title":"Kinetic theoretical study of a simply sheared two-dimensional granular gas to Burnett order","volume":"8","author":"Sela","year":"1996","journal-title":"Phys. Fluids"},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref30","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"187","DOI":"10.1017\/S0022112083001044","article-title":"Theory for the rapid flow of identical, smooth, nearly elastic, spherical particles","volume":"130","author":"Jenkins","year":"1983","journal-title":"J. Fluid Mech."},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref47","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"179","DOI":"10.1017\/S0022112097005648","article-title":"Instabilities of fully developed rapid flow of a granular material in a channel","volume":"342","author":"Wang","year":"1997","journal-title":"J. Fluid Mech."},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref26","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"103307","DOI":"10.1063\/1.2364168","article-title":"Dense shearing flows of inelastic disks","volume":"18","author":"Jenkins","year":"2006","journal-title":"Phys. Fluids"},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref48","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1174","DOI":"10.1002\/aic.16026","article-title":"DEM study on the discharge characteristics of lognormal particle size distributions from a conical hopper","volume":"64","author":"Zhao","year":"2018","journal-title":"AIChE J."},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref42","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"53","DOI":"10.1017\/S0022112079000525","article-title":"Gravity flow of cohesionless granular materials in chutes and channels","volume":"92","author":"Savage","year":"1979","journal-title":"J. Fluid Mech."},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"69","DOI":"10.1017\/S0022112008002358","article-title":"Kinematics and statistics of dense, slow granular flow thro