-page":"441","DOI":"10.1142\/S0219525901000358","article-title":"Slow dense granular flows as a self-induced process","volume":"4","author":"Pouliquen","year":"2001","journal-title":"Adv. Complex Syst."},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref18","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"149","DOI":"10.1007\/s10035-010-0204-9","article-title":"Discrete element modelling of grain flow in a planar silo: influence of simulation parameters","volume":"13","author":"Gonz\u00e1lez-Montellano","year":"2011","journal-title":"Granular Matter"},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"49","DOI":"10.1098\/rspa.1954.0186","article-title":"Experiments on a gravity-free dispersion of large solid spheres in a Newtonian fluid under shear","volume":"225","author":"Bagnold","year":"1954","journal-title":"Proc. R. Soc. Lond. A"},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref6","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"094303","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevFluids.3.094303","article-title":"Fluidity, anisotropy, and velocity correlations in frictionless, collisional grain flows","volume":"3","author":"Berzi","year":"2018","journal-title":"Phys. Rev. Fluids"},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref15","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"5895","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevE.59.5895","article-title":"Dense fluid transport for inelastic hard spheres","volume":"59","author":"Garz\u00f3","year":"1999","journal-title":"Phys. Rev. E"},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref3","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"219","DOI":"10.1098\/rspa.1966.0236","article-title":"The shearing and dilatation of dry sand and the \u2018singing\u2019 mechanism","volume":"295","author":"Bagnold","year":"1966","journal-title":"Proc. R. Soc. Lond. A"},{"key":"S0022112022008072_ref17","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"56","DOI":"10.1007\/s10035-017-0738-1","article-title":"Extended kinetic theory applied to inclined granular flows: role of boundaries","volume":"19","author":"Gollin","year":"2017","journal-title":"Granul